  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A memory card can be left beside the exhibit or discussed with a volunteer.\", \"decision\": \"How should visitors share a memory linked to an exhibit?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVisitors discuss a memory with a volunteer and then choose what to put on a card. Conversation can help them shape the written account.\nVisitors write a memory card first and choose whether to discuss it with a volunteer. They can decide what to share before a conversation.\nVisitors and a volunteer fill out a memory card together during the conversation. The written account develops with immediate clarification."
    }
